# Erlang VM flags for the release. `#` starts a comment.

# The relx start script refuses to boot without exactly one of -name/-sname,
# so distribution cannot simply be left off. 127.0.0.1 always resolves, so the
# release starts the same way in Docker, in CI and on a workstation.
-name kv_store@127.0.0.1

# Confine the distribution listener to loopback. By default it binds every
# interface, which would let any peer that can reach the container network
# attempt a handshake. Nothing here uses rpc, net_kernel or global, so the
# listener exists only to satisfy the start script.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

# No -setcookie: with none given the VM generates a random cookie in
# $HOME/.erlang.cookie at first boot. A literal here would be a shared secret
# committed to the repository and baked into every published image.

# Skip crash dump generation rather than only redirecting it. Setting
# ERL_CRASH_DUMP alone still walks every process and formats the whole dump
# before writing it, which just delays the restart.
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS 0
